// Manually Modifying a Binary to add Encryption:

Get enctest // or your chosen program
riscv32-unknown-elf-objcopy enctest --dump-section .text=text.dump // Dumps the code section
xxd -p text.dump > hex.txt // Gets the dump into just hex text which can be read and modified
Make your modifications // The modifications I made to enctest are recorded in EncTestFilesandNotes
./converter // This is in the HextoDumpConverter file, converting.cpp is the original code
Copy the relevant section from text-mod.dump, w/o the extra around space at the end
printf "[dump section here, dont include the brackets]" >> textfinal.dump
riscv32-unknown-elf-objcopy enctest --update-section .text=textfinal.dump

